1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bc4 Bc5 4. b4 { The Evans Gambit: a wing pawn to gain time for c3 and d4. }
4... Bxb4 { [%name Accepted, 5...Ba5] }
( 4... Bb6 { [%name Declined] }
  5. a4 { Threatening a5 to trap the bishop. }
  5... a6 6. Nc3 Nf6 7. Nd5 Nxd5 8. exd5 Nd4 9. a5 Ba7 10. d6 { Breaking up Black's pawns before the a7 bishop becomes active. } )
5. c3 { Gaining a tempo on the bishop and preparing d4. }
5... Ba5
( 5... Be7 { [%name 5...Be7] }
  6. d4 Na5 7. Nxe5 { Winning back the pawn; the c4 bishop is left for the knight. }
  7... Nxc4 8. Nxc4 d5 9. exd5 Qxd5 10. Ne3 { Gaining time on the queen; White has a healthy centre. } )
6. d4 { Opening the centre while Black's king is still in the middle. }
6... exd4 7. O-O { Development first: the pawn can wait. }
7... Nge7 8. cxd4 d5 9. exd5 Nxd5 10. Ba3 { The bishop stops Black from castling short. } *
